<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $22.9 mln Nov 7.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $22.9 mln Nov 7.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $22.9 million surplus on November 7 according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 7</p>
<p>Exports: $146.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $165.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $217.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $175.7 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $22.9 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $900 million</p>
<p>Imports: $836 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.198 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.110 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.152 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-248-5415</p>
</text>
